# openElement starter

Start the dev server and open the URL it prints.

```sh
npm run dev
```

Edit the heading in `app/routes/index.tsx` and save. The dev server updates the
home page. Then try the counter in `app/islands/my-counter.tsx` or add a route
under `app/routes/`.

Use Node.js 24.2 or newer. The scaffold pins the recommended development
version in `.node-version`. If you skipped installation, run the install
command printed by the CLI first. Use the same package manager for installs
and scripts.

## Find the examples

| Path                         | What it does                                                   |
| ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `app/routes/index.tsx`       | Prerenders `/` and hosts the counter and timer.                |
| `app/islands/my-counter.tsx` | Renders the counter on the server and hydrates on idle.        |
| `app/islands/live-timer.tsx` | Mounts the timer in the browser with `ssr: false`.             |
| `app/routes/about.tsx`       | Prerenders `/about` without islands of its own.                |
| `app/routes/api/ping.ts`     | Serves JSON from the request-time route `/api/ping`.           |
| `app/routes/404.tsx`         | Renders the fallback page for unmatched paths.                 |
| `app/layout.tsx`             | Wraps every page in the shared header, main region and footer. |
| `app/styles/theme.css`       | Defines the palette and Tailwind theme tokens.                 |
| `app/head.tsx`               | Adds shared metadata and links to the document head.           |

A page with no islands of its own can still load the app-wide claim bootstrap
when other pages in the app use islands.

## Scripts

- `npm test` checks the ping route with the Node.js test runner.
- `npm run typecheck` type-checks application code, tests and configuration.
- `npm run fmt` formats the source. `npm run lint` checks it.
- `npm run build` writes the public upload directory `dist-public/` and the request-time server in `dist/server/`. Run `npx oe publish --check` before uploading public files.
- `npm start` serves the production build.

Framework options live in `openelement.config.ts`. Vite configuration lives in
`vite.config.ts`. The router writes its working files to `.openElement/` and
recreates the directory as needed.

To create another project, use `npm create @openelement <project-name>`.
[Documentation](https://openelement.org)
